 ## Status (as of hand-off)
 - Both branches merged. `exp/vectorized-join` merged first (conflict: PROGRESS.md only; its EXPERIMENT.md/PROGRESS.md moved to docs/vectorized-join-*.md). `exp/columnar-storage` merged second (conflicts: PROGRESS.md + src/query/patterns/triple.rs, the latter in `estimate_count`/`create_iterator`; both sides kept — columnar rewrites AE/AV prefixes onto AEV/AVE segments and swaps in SegmentIterator, and since the batched path calls the SAME two helpers, the batch engine becomes columnar-aware for free).
 - `cargo check --all-targets` clean after each merge.
+- Bench: 4 arms (off / batched / columnar / all) x 3 passes, interleaved. JSON in results/combo-vec-col-{off,batched,columnar,all}.json. Row counts identical in all four arms and equal to baseline.
+- all/off medians: triangles 0.35, two_hop 0.40, three_hop 0.25, out_degree 0.18, in_degree_top 0.19, neighbors_of_42 0.06, weight_filter 0.17, weight_sum 0.19, heavy_neighbors 0.21, label_lookup 0.69 (noise).
+- three_hop: columnar alone regresses (1.07x med / 1.27x min); all/batched is 0.70 med / 0.93 min, so batching removes the regression. Mechanism: grouped_extensions sorts seeks ascending, SegmentIterator::seek reuses the already-decoded segment.
+- Tests: off and batched-alone fully green; columnar-alone and all-on both fail the same 11 lib tests (10 documented by the columnar branch + the batched equivalence test, which seeds raw row keys and so dies on 'bad segment header' under columnar alone). clippy clean off and all-on; fmt clean.
 
